{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. Title 23 BUILDINGS AND CONSTRUCTION Chapter 23.04 NUMBERING BUILDINGS \u00a7\u00a7 23.04.010 \u2013 23.04.100 Chapter 23.06 ADMINISTRATIVE CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.06.010 \u2013 23.06.120 Chapter 23.07 RESIDENTIAL CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.07.010 \u2013 23.07.110 Chapter 23.08 BUILDING CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.08.010 \u2013 23.08.170 Chapter 23.09 EXISTING BUILDING CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.09.010 \u2013 23.09.010 Chapter 23.10 EARTHQUAKE HAZARD REDUCTION CODE [Repealed] Chapter 23.12 ELECTRICAL CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.12.010 \u2013 23.12.010 Chapter 23.16 PLUMBING CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.16.010 \u2013 23.16.020 Chapter 23.20 MECHANICAL CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.20.010 \u2013 23.20.010 Chapter 23.24 ENERGY CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.24.010 \u2013 23.24.010 Chapter 23.28 FIRE CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.28.010 \u2013 23.28.250 Chapter 23.30 Dangerous Building Code \u00a7\u00a7 23.30.010 \u2013 23.30.080 Chapter 23.32 FIRE PROTECTION FACILITIES CODE [Repealed] Chapter 23.33 FLOODPLAIN MANAGEMENT \u00a7\u00a7 23.33.010 \u2013 23.33.070 Chapter 23.36 Historical Building Code \u00a7\u00a7 23.36.010 \u2013 23.36.010 Chapter 23.38 Referenced Standards Code \u00a7\u00a7 23.38.010 \u2013 23.38.010 Chapter 23.40 SITE DEVELOPMENT CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.40.010 \u2013 23.40.050 Chapter 23.44 ELECTRIC VEHICLE CHARGING STATIONS \u00a7\u00a7 23.44.020 \u2013 23.44.060 Chapter 23.46 SMALL RESIDENTIAL ROOFTOP SOLAR ENERGY SYSTEMS \u00a7\u00a7 23.46.010 \u2013 23.46.070 Chapter 23.48 SPECIFICATIONS FOR PUBLIC WORKS CONSTRUCTION \u00a7\u00a7 23.48.010 \u2013 23.48.040 Chapter 23.50 ACCESS COMPLIANCE \u00a7\u00a7 23.50.010 \u2013 23.50.010 Chapter 23.54 BUILDING SECURITY CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.54.005 \u2013 23.54.130 Chapter 23.56 MOVING BUILDING CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.56.010 \u2013 23.56.040 Chapter 23.58 VISIBILITY IN BARS \u00a7\u00a7 23.58.010 \u2013 23.58.030 Chapter 23.60 ART IN PUBLIC PLACES \u00a7\u00a7 23.60.010 \u2013 23.60.140 Chapter 23.61 AFFORDABLE HOUSING COMMERCIAL LINKAGE FEE \u00a7\u00a7 23.61.010 \u2013 23.61.080 Chapter 23.65 Child Care Development Fee \u00a7\u00a7 23.65.010 \u2013 23.65.020 Chapter 23.70 GREEN BUILDING CODE \u00a7\u00a7 23.70.010 \u2013 23.70.090 Chapter 23.72 WATER CONSERVATION IN LANDSCAPING \u00a7\u00a7 23.72.010 \u2013 23.72.200", "num": "23", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23", "title": "Title 23 BUILDINGS AND CONSTRUCTION", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. Chapter 23.04 NUMBERING BUILDINGS 23.04.010 DEFINITIONS. 23.04.020 RECORDS. 23.04.030 NUMBERING SYSTEM ESTABLISHED. 23.04.040 ENTRANCES\u2014CORRECT NUMBER REQUIRED. 23.04.050 OBTAINING CORRECT NUMBER. 23.04.060 ODD AND EVEN NUMBERS. 23.04.070 NUMBERS ALLOTTED TO NORMAL BLOCK. 23.04.080 NUMBER ALLOTMENT WHERE THERE ARE NO NORMAL BLOCKS. 23.04.090 COST OF RENUMBERING. 23.04.100 STARTING POINTS DESIGNATED.", "num": "23.04", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04", "title": "Chapter 23.04 NUMBERING BUILDINGS", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.010 DEFINITIONS. The following definitions shall apply to words used in this chapter : (a) \"Building\" means a residential, commercial, industrial or other building or structure, including, but not limited to, fences, gates, and appurtenances, located on any premises; (b) \"Normal block\" means a block in which a street is intersected by other streets at regular intervals of not to exceed six hundred feet; (c) \"Owner\" means the owner, tenant, occupant or person in control of the premises in question; (d) \"Street\" means a public easement for travel purposes, including, but not limited to, alleys, highways, courts, avenues, streets and boulevards. (Prior code \u00a7 157.01.)", "num": "23.04.010", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.010", "title": "23.04.010 DEFINITIONS.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.020", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.020 RECORDS. The Superintendent of Streets shall at all times keep on file in his or her office a book or card index containing the official street number of each building within the City. (Prior code \u00a7 157.02.)", "num": "23.04.020", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.020", "title": "23.04.020 RECORDS.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.020"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.030", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.030 NUMBERING SYSTEM ESTABLISHED. A system for the numbering of buildings and structures in this city is established and shall be maintained in and for the City. (Prior code \u00a7 157.03.)", "num": "23.04.030", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.030", "title": "23.04.030 NUMBERING SYSTEM ESTABLISHED.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.030"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.040", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.040 ENTRANCES\u2014CORRECT NUMBER REQUIRED. No owner may place, maintain or allow to remain thereon any number other than such number as herein required, or permit any such building or structure having an entrance from a public street to remain unnumbered. (a) Entrances from streets to buildings must be numbered at the expense of the owner. All residential buildings shall display a street number in a prominent location on the street side of the building in such a position that the number is readily visible from approaching emergency vehicles. The numerals shall be not less than four (4) inches in height for single family and residential buildings and not less than six (6) inches in height for all other buildings. Numerals, letters or other identifications shall be used to identify individual residential units, offices or other spaces within a building and shall not be less than four (4) inches in height. All numerals or other identification shall be of contrasting color to the background surface to which they are attached and shall be illuminated during the hours of darkness when located at the exterior of the building. (Ord. No. 2008-8 \u00a7 17; Ord. No. 2007-16 \u00a7 2; Prior code \u00a7 157.05.)", "num": "23.04.040", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.040", "title": "23.04.040 ENTRANCES\u2014CORRECT NUMBER REQUIRED.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.040"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.050", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.050 OBTAINING CORRECT NUMBER. The Superintendent of Streets, upon request, shall inform the owner of any building of the correct number which should be placed thereon. (Ord. No. 2007-16 \u00a7 2; Prior code \u00a7 157.06.)", "num": "23.04.050", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.050", "title": "23.04.050 OBTAINING CORRECT NUMBER.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.050"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.060", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.060 ODD AND EVEN NUMBERS. Numbers on the right side of the street from the point of beginning shall be even numbers, and the numbers of the left side thereof shall be odd numbers. (Ord. No. 2007-16 \u00a7 2; Prior code \u00a7 157.07.)", "num": "23.04.060", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.060", "title": "23.04.060 ODD AND EVEN NUMBERS.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.060"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.070", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.070 NUMBERS ALLOTTED TO NORMAL BLOCK. One hundred numbers shall be allotted to each normal block and shall be evenly divided in units of street frontage. (Ord. No. 2007-16 \u00a7 2; Prior code \u00a7 157.08.)", "num": "23.04.070", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.070", "title": "23.04.070 NUMBERS ALLOTTED TO NORMAL BLOCK.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.070"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.080", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.080 NUMBER ALLOTMENT WHERE THERE ARE NO NORMAL BLOCKS. In the event that a street is not intersected at regular intervals by other streets and is not therefore a normal block, numbers shall be allotted in the same manner as if it were intersected at such regular intervals. (Ord. No. 2007-16 \u00a7 2; Prior code \u00a7 157.09.)", "num": "23.04.080", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.080", "title": "23.04.080 NUMBER ALLOTMENT WHERE THERE ARE NO NORMAL BLOCKS.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.080"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.090", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.090 COST OF RENUMBERING. Whenever, by reason of any new building being erected or altered, it becomes necessary to renumber any block now numbered, it shall be the obligation of the owner requesting the assignment of a new number or numbers to pay the cost of renumbering the entire block. (Ord. No. 2007-16 \u00a7 2; Prior code \u00a7 157.10.)", "num": "23.04.090", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.090", "title": "23.04.090 COST OF RENUMBERING.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.090"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.100", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.04.100 STARTING POINTS DESIGNATED. Baywood Avenue, Baldwin Avenue, San Mateo Creek and Cypress Avenue, for streets running in a generally northerly and southerly direction, and El Camino Real, for streets running in a general easterly and westerly direction, shall be the starting points for the numbers on streets beginning thereat or intersecting or crossing same; provided that streets running in a general northerly and southerly direction, but not intersecting or crossing Baywood Avenue, Baldwin Avenue or San Mateo Creek will be numbered as if they commenced thereat, so as to correspond with other streets which do commence thereat or run therefrom; provided also that streets running in a general easterly and westerly direction, and not intersecting or crossing El Camino Real, will be numbered as if they commenced thereat, and so as to correspond with the numbering on other streets which do commence thereat or run therefrom. El Camino Real, and other generally parallel streets easterly therefrom shall be numbered so as to correspond with generally parallel streets westerly therefrom. Numbers on streets bearing the same name north and south of Baldwin Avenue, San Mateo Creek or Cypress Avenue shall be designated as numbered \"north\" and \"south\" respectively therefrom. Numbers on streets bearing the same name east and west of El Camino Real shall be designated as numbered \"east\" and \"west\" respectively therefrom. On other intermediate or subdivision streets not otherwise provided for, numbering shall proceed in the same direction as, and in block numbers corresponding with, the numbering on the principal streets between which they lie, and which run generally in the same direction. (Ord. No. 2007-16 \u00a7 2; Prior code \u00a7 157.11.)", "num": "23.04.100", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.04|23.04.100", "title": "23.04.100 STARTING POINTS DESIGNATED.", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.04.100"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.06", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. Chapter 23.06 ADMINISTRATIVE CODE 23.06.010 Adoption 23.06.011 APPLICATION TO EXISTING BUILDINGS AND BUILDING SERVICE EQUIPMENT. [Repealed] 23.06.012 DEFINITIONS. [Repealed] 23.06.013 CONFLICTING PROVISIONS. 23.06.014 ALTERNATE MATERIALS, METHODS OF DESIGN AND METHODS OF CONSTRUCTION. [Repealed] 23.06.015 MODIFICATIONS. [Repealed] 23.06.016 TESTS. [Repealed] 23.06.017 TEMPORARY BUILDING. 23.06.020 AUTHORITY. [Repealed] 23.06.021 POWERS AND DUTIES OF BUILDING OFFICIAL. [Repealed] 23.06.030 UNSAFE BUILDINGS, STRUCTURES OR BUILDING SERVICE EQUIPMENT. [Repealed] 23.06.040 APPEALS. [Repealed] 23.06.050 VIOLATIONS AND PENALTIES. [Repealed] 23.06.060 Hours of Work 23.06.061 Hours of Work Exemption 23.06.070 PERMITS. [Repealed] 23.06.080 APPLICATION FOR PERMIT. [Repealed] 23.06.090 PERMITS ISSUANCE. [Repealed] 23.06.100 Demolition Permits 23.06.110 INSPECTIONS. [Repealed] 23.06.120 Fees 23.06.130 SPECIAL INSPECTIONS. [Repealed] 23.06.140 STRUCTURAL OBSERVATION. [Repealed] 23.06.150 CONNECTION TO UTILITIES. [Repealed] 23.06.160 CERTIFICATE OF OCCUPANCY. [Repealed] 23.06.170 FIRE AND HEALTH PROTECTION. [Repealed]", "num": "23.06", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.06", "title": "Chapter 23.06 ADMINISTRATIVE CODE", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.06"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.06.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.06.010 Adoption a. The 2022 California Administrative Code, California Code of Regulations, Title 24, Part 1, as adopted and amended by the State of California, hereinafter called \"Administrative Code,\" is adopted as the rules, regulations, and standards within this City as to all matters therein except as hereinafter modified or amended. b. No section of the Administrative Code shall impose a mandatory duty of enforcement on the City, or on any officer, official, agent, employee, board, council, or commission thereof. Instead, if any section purports to impose a mandatory duty of enforcement, that section shall invest the City, and the appropriate officer, official, agent, employee, board, council or commission with discretion to enforce the section, or not to enforce it. c. A copy of the Administrative Code shall at all times be kept on file in the office of the City Clerk. ( Ord. No. 2022-11 \u00a7 1 ; Ord. No. 2019-13 \u00a7 1(b) ; Ord. No. 2016-10 \u00a7 1 ; Ord. No. 2013-13 \u00a7 1 ; Ord. No. 2010-16 \u00a7 1 ; Ord. No. 2007-11 \u00a7 1; Ord. No. 1999-8 \u00a7 2; Ord. No. 1992-12 \u00a7 1; Ord. No. 1990-1 \u00a7 1; Ord. No. 1988-4 \u00a7 1; Ord. No. 1985-4 \u00a7 1; Ord. No. 1981-4 \u00a7 1.)", "num": "23.06.010", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.06|23.06.010", "title": "23.06.010 Adoption", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.06.010"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.06.011", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.06.011 APPLICATION TO EXISTING BUILDINGS AND BUILDING SERVICE EQUIPMENT. [Repealed] Repealed. ( Ord. No. 2019-13 \u00a7 1(a) ; Ord. No. 2016-10 \u00a7 1 ; Ord. No. 2013-13 \u00a7 1 ; Ord. No. 2010-16 \u00a7 1 ; Ord. No. 2007-11 \u00a7 1.)", "num": "23.06.011", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.06|23.06.011", "title": "23.06.011 APPLICATION TO EXISTING BUILDINGS AND BUILDING SERVICE EQUIPMENT.\n[Repealed]", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.06.011"}
