{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. Chapter 23.24 ENERGY CODE 23.24.010 Adoption 23.24.020 Local Amendment to Definitions [Repealed] 23.24.030 Local Amendment Regarding Mandatory Solar Installations [Repealed] 23.24.040 Local Amendment Regarding All-Electric Requirements for Residential Buildings and Buildings with Office Use. [Repealed] 23.24.050 Local Amendment Regarding All-Electric or Energy Efficiency Standards for High-Rise Multifamily Residential Buildings with 100% Affordable Units. [Repealed] 23.24.060 Local Amendment Regarding All-Electric Buildings or Energy Efficiency Standards for Low-Rise Residential Buildings with 100% Affordable Units. [Repealed] 23.24.070 Infeasibility Exemption. [Repealed] 23.24.080 Expiration. [Repealed]", "num": "23.24", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.24", "title": "Chapter 23.24 ENERGY CODE", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.24"}
{"index": {"_id": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.24.010", "_type": "page"}}
{"body": "City of San Mateo Municipal Code. 23.24.010 Adoption (a) The California Energy Code, 2022 Edition, Title 24, Part 6 of the California Code of Regulations, as adopted and amended by the State of California, hereinafter called \"Energy Code,\" is adopted as the rules, regulations and standards within this City as to all matters therein except as hereinafter modified or amended. (b) One copy of the Energy Code shall at all times be kept on file in the office of the City Clerk. ( Ord. No. 2022-13 \u00a7 1 ; Ord. No. 2019-9 \u00a7 1 ; Ord. No. 2016-5 \u00a7 1 .)", "num": "23.24.010", "path": "library|City of San Mateo, Cal., Code|23|23.24|23.24.010", "title": "23.24.010 Adoption", "url": "/us/ca/cities/san-mateo/code/23.24.010"}
